<main>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">How it works</p>
      <h1>From sign-up to <em>release day</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">RRR is a community label. You pay a small monthly membership, book releases for a one-off upload fee, and keep 100% of your royalties.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="side">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="side-head"><span class="tag">A</span><h2>For artists</h2></div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><div><h3>Create your account</h3><p>Join as an artist for <span data-price="artist">€2.00</span> a month. You get community membership, promotion opportunities and your own digital Synth Stars card, with the option to order a printed card plus postage. <a href="index.html#join">Create account</a></p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Link your Bandcamp and Spotify</h3><p>Link your Bandcamp account to the RRR label so sales go straight to you: that is how you keep 100%. Choose <a href="series.html#linking">password linking</a> (recommended: full promotion and stats) or a Bandcamp invite. When your Bandcamp is linked to the RRR Bandcamp, you get <b>free Bandcamp VIP membership</b> for as long as your releases stay active in the catalogue. (Bandcamp VIP is separate from membership of this platform.) You can also add RRR to your Spotify for Artists team as your label so we can help manage it.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Book your release</h3><p>Pick a release date in the RRR release calendar (dates are subject to availability) and choose Bandcamp, streaming or both. Upload fees: single <span data-price="single">€2.00</span>, EP (2–5 tracks) <span data-price="ep">€2.50</span>, album <span data-price="album">€3.00</span>. One fee covers Bandcamp, streaming or both. <a href="book.html#bandcamp">Book a release</a></p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Send your assets on time</h3><p>Put your audio, artwork and release details in your designated Google Drive folder at least <b>3 weeks</b> before release for streaming and at least <b>2 weeks</b> before for Bandcamp. See the <a href="release-policy.html">release policy</a> for exactly what to send.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Release day</h3><p>Your release goes live on your Bandcamp page and the RRR page, and on streaming through the RRR RouteNote account. Bandcamp sales are paid on to your PayPal on the 30th of each month, with a statement of every sale (minus only Bandcamp's and PayPal's standard charges; RRR takes nothing). Streaming royalties are paid through your free RouteNote account about every 45 days.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Pitch to editors yourself</h3><p>Bandcamp and Spotify editorial pitching is done by you, not RRR. Follow the <a href="editorial.html">editorial guides</a>: Bandcamp 8–9 weeks ahead, Spotify at least 7 days ahead.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Promote it with the community</h3><p>Book a promotional post on RRR social media, upload a video to the RRR YouTube channel, and submit to The Bandcamp Hour through Groover. <a href="book.html">See booking options</a></p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="side">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="side-head"><span class="tag">B</span><h2>For fans</h2></div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><div><h3>Join as a fan</h3><p>Fan membership is <span data-price="fan">€1.00</span> a month and lets you collect your favourite artists' Synth Stars cards, digital or printed plus postage. <a href="index.html#join">Create account</a></p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Get close to the artists</h3><p>Talk directly with RRR artists and take part in community events and activities.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Support and earn</h3><p>Buy music, share releases and help other members to earn community points and a shot at Fan of the Month.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="side">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="side-head"><h2>Common questions</h2></div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details class="panel"><summary>Is RRR exclusive?</summary><p>No. RRR membership is non-exclusive. Release independently when you want, work with other labels when you want, and release selected projects through RRR when it makes sense. Only releases you choose to submit, and that RRR approves, become RRR releases. <a href="series.html">About Selected Releases</a></p></details>
        <details class="panel"><summary>How long does a release stay in the RRR catalogue?</summary><p>On Bandcamp, <b>permanently</b>, through the permanent link. It costs nothing and every sale is still 100% yours. On streaming, RRR is the only distributor for <b>18 months</b>, because a second upload gets flagged and removed. After that, ask and we take it down from streaming so you can re-upload it yourself. Bandcamp and YouTube are never exclusive, and remixes, edits and new versions are yours to release anywhere, any time. Tracks on RRR compilations stay there permanently, and we always ask before adding one. <a href="terms.html#t3">Full terms</a></p></details>
        <details class="panel"><summary>Do I keep my royalties?</summary><p>Yes. You keep 100% of your royalties from Bandcamp and streaming releases made through RRR (Bandcamp still takes its usual sales fee), and you keep ownership of your music and intellectual property.</p></details>
        <details class="panel"><summary>What if I need a break?</summary><p>Switch to Community Supporter Status: <span data-price="supporterArtist">€1.00</span> a month for artists, <span data-price="supporterFan">€0.50</span> for fans. You keep your membership, rank, points and achievements, but can't book releases or promotions until you reactivate. You can reactivate at any time.</p></details>
        <details class="panel"><summary>Can RRR run offers on my release?</summary><p>Yes. Releases in the RRR Bandcamp catalogue can be included in RRR discount codes, giveaways and promotional offers. This is a condition of the Bandcamp service.</p></details>
        <details class="panel"><summary>How do I pay?</summary><p>Everything is paid by PayPal, which also takes debit and credit cards. Membership is a monthly PayPal subscription you set up right after signing up. One-off fees, like release and YouTube uploads, are paid after you book. Payment opens when sign-up launches.</p></details>
        <details class="panel"><summary>Where do I see my achievements?</summary><p>Every member gets a member ID when they sign up. It opens your <a href="member.html">member dashboard</a>: rank, points, achievements, releases, social posts and stats.</p></details>
        <details class="panel"><summary>Who do I contact?</summary><p>Email <span id="hiw-email">retroreverbrecords@gmail.com</span> <button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="hiw-email">Copy</button></p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
